
=== Exact byte boundary and actionable splitting instructions ===
$ git -C boundary 'init' '-q'
exit=0

$ git -C boundary 'config' 'core.hooksPath' '.githooks'
exit=0

write boundary/'exact.txt': 20000 bytes, header=b''
$ git -C boundary 'add' '--' 'exact.txt'
exit=0

$ git -C boundary 'rev-parse' '--verify' 'HEAD'
exit=128
fatal: Needed a single revision

$ git -C boundary 'commit' '-m' 'exactly 5000 tokens allowed'
exit=0
[master (root-commit) 3a73079] exactly 5000 tokens allowed
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
 create mode 100644 exact.txt

$ git -C boundary 'rev-parse' '--verify' 'HEAD'
exit=0
3a73079503c21f141db84df7d289e681a6d556bb

$ git -C boundary 'ls-tree' '-rl' 'HEAD'
exit=0
100644 blob 7eded2aa2b98c9f0d9d4bb82c277cbbd09dcd044   20000	exact.txt

write boundary/'new.txt': 20001 bytes, header=b''
$ git -C boundary 'add' '--' 'new.txt'
exit=0

$ git -C boundary 'rev-parse' '--verify' 'HEAD'
exit=0
3a73079503c21f141db84df7d289e681a6d556bb

$ git -C boundary 'commit' '-m' 'one byte above cap refused'
exit=1
precommit-token-cap: 1 staged file(s) exceed the 5000-token limit (tokens = bytes/4)

  new.txt: 20001 bytes = 5001 tokens (limit 5000)

How to split:
  1. Split along existing responsibility boundaries - one concern per file.
  2. Move helpers or sections into sibling files with the same naming convention.
  3. Keep a thin entry point that sources or imports them, then update references and tests.
  4. For documentation, split by heading into linked pages.

An already-oversized existing file only has to stop growing: staging it at the same size or smaller passes, and splitting or shrinking it still helps.

$ git -C boundary 'rev-parse' '--verify' 'HEAD'
exit=0
3a73079503c21f141db84df7d289e681a6d556bb


